cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below. You are never required to cite it to use or teach from it."
title: "Python for Biochemical Data and Enzyme Kinetics"
abstract: >-
  An intermediate open course on fitting enzyme kinetics without fooling yourself: the
  Michaelis-Menten model, the measured cost of linearising it, weighting and error models,
  bootstrap uncertainty, AICc model comparison, inhibition mechanisms and calibration with
  detection limits. Includes a tested teaching package (kinetics), six modules, five guided
  practicals, a quiz with answer key, an instructor pack and simulated datasets with recorded
  seeds and error models. Part of the CLS-Open initiative of fifteen interlinked computational
  life-sciences courses.
